<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Argentine telcoms raised.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Argentine telcoms raised.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Salomon Brothers analysts Sari Mayer and Andres Pitchon raised their ratings for Telecom Argentina and Telefonica de Argentina Wednesday to buy from hold.</p>
<p>-- They based their upgrade on a ruling by an Argentine court that lets Telefonica de Argentina bill under a new rate structure.  The decision effectively eliminates the need for a Supreme Court ruling on the issue soon.</p>
<p>-- Telecom's American Depositary Receipt (ADR) was down 3/8 to 56-1/8. Telefonica's ADR was unchanged at 38-1/2.</p>
<p>((--Ian Simpson, Wall Street desk, (212) 859-1879))</p>
